So my idea for tab AI completition is this:
I will write metaprogram tags in comments around a funciton or a block of code. When I press a specific keybind we will send the buffer info to a FIM LLM or a general purpose chat completitions LLM and insert the thing it returns in the block.

Preaty simple but I want to make it powerful and good looking with these things:
1. We will have a solit animation for it. We will use the node installintion 2x3 dots rectenge thing that indicates loading while we are waiting the request and we will have an option for streaming=True and we will get the code written in front of our eyes. If streaming=False just loading until full responce ready than paste it right in.
2. Metatags. We will define our custom language to give more context and specification to the AI. We will use the treesitter/LSP knwleadge for knowing what is a comment in the current buffer and after a comment we will put @<name_of_tag>. (if we don't know the comment type for the current file we will deafult to "--- @" but for a C/Java like we will have "// @" or python "# @" and so on. Right now the tags I have in mind are:
